{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"DRIVE_FORGE|drive_forge_poll|returned verify|forge-unconcluded|forge checks are not green|ready to merge\\\" /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/templates /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema; sed -n '1,125p' /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo; sed -n '260,310p' /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo; sed -n '540,590p' /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo; sed -n '8360,8695p' /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmpd60f3o1z/diff.patch\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:187:verify with the forge still green prints that the item is ready to merge\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:206:passing step, until the item is ready to merge or a step stops on its\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:276:DRIVE_FORGE_POLL_BOUND_DEFAULT_S = 600.0\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:277:DRIVE_FORGE_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT_S = 20.0\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:280:def drive_forge_poll_bound_s() -> float:\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:281:    return float(os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S\", DRIVE_FORGE_POLL_BOUND_DEFAULT_S))\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:284:def drive_forge_poll_interval_s() -> float:\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:285:    return float(os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S\", DRIVE_FORGE_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT_S))\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:538:STOP_CLASSES = (\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"no-cause\", \"forge-unconcluded\",\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:675:      - a returned verify (the forge was not green; no adapter ran) is\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:676:        forge-unconcluded/tenant\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:688:        return {\"class\": \"forge-unconcluded\", \"provenance\": \"tenant\", \"detail\": None}\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:1904:# adapter's own pre-emptive refusal, forge-unconcluded from a returned\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:1913:GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES = (\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"forge-unconcluded\", \"ceiling\",\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:2456:        print(f\"attavo verify: returned ({record_path.name}); the forge checks are not green\")\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:2746:    \"\"\"read_forge_checks, retried within drive_forge_poll_bound_s() while\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:2755:    bound = drive_forge_poll_bound_s()\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:2756:    interval = drive_forge_poll_interval_s()\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:2980:    print(f\"attavo drive: item {item_id} is ready to merge\")\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:2988:    # drive: item N is ready to merge -- would otherwise sit unflushed\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo:3015:    # item is ready to merge or a step stops on its own account.\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/verify.schema.json:113:          \"enum\": [\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"no-cause\", \"forge-unconcluded\",\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/build.schema.json:111:          \"enum\": [\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"no-cause\", \"forge-unconcluded\",\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/counsel.schema.json:59:      \"enum\": [\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"no-cause\", \"forge-unconcluded\",\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"attavo: the command.\n\n    attavo doctor [TENANT_ROOT] [--json]\n    attavo spec-gate [N]\n    attavo approve [N] --by LOGIN\n    attavo approval-status [N]\n    attavo build [N]\n    attavo verify [N]\n    attavo file-findings [N]\n    attavo file-stops [N]\n    attavo counsel [N]\n    attavo record-only\n    attavo attest [--partial] [N]\n    attavo drive [N] [--until-ready]\n    attavo ledger [N] [--json]\n    attavo stops [N] [--json]\n\nThe doctor is the definition of done. It asserts four proofs against a\ntenant root and exits 1 until every proof holds:\n\n  1. every-gate-rejects      every gate in the manifest's [gates] table,\n                             run against its rejection fixture, exits non-zero,\n                             and carries a non-empty retires\n  2. one-item-every-stage    one work item under paths.records carries a\n                             record for every stage -- spec, approval,\n                             build, verify -- all four introduced by one\n                             merge commit reachable from HEAD\n  3. no-commit-lacks-record  every commit on the default branch after the\n                             manifest was introduced is named by a record's\n                             sha or commits list, or itself writes under\n                             paths.records (a record is committed with the\n                             code it describes; an item's merge commit\n                             carries its own record paths this way)\n  4. no-stop-lacks-cause     every build or verify record under\n                             paths.records at record_version 3 or later,\n                             with a status other than pass, carries a stop\n                             naming an enumerated class and provenance, a\n                             non-empty detail when unclassed, the gates\n                             heading when a build failed after running\n                             them, and the tool's own error line when an\n                             adapter exit ended the log -- records before\n                             record_version 3 are counted and reported,\n                             never refused\n\nNothing in doctor is a gate. The doctor reads; it never writes and it never\nblocks a merge by itself. It is what CI runs to say whether the product\nis done.\n\nspec-gate, approve, and approval-status are gates and writers. They run\nfrom the tenant root (the current working directory); N, the work item id,\nis read from the ATTAVO_ITEM environment variable when set, else from the\nbranch (attavo/N-*). The doctor's first proof sets ATTAVO_ITEM for a\nrejection fixture's own item, so a gate's own command needs no argument\neven while the enclosing repository sits on a real item's attavo/N-*\nbranch. Every run of spec-gate or approve writes the next numbered attempt\nfile under paths.records/N/ and never overwrites one already written. See\nthe spec contract in the project's Phase 1 issue for the full rules each\none enforces.\n\nbuild refuses (exit 1, naming the cause, no record) unless the manifest\ndeclares [executor].build and [tests].select and [tests].run, and unless\napproval-status would print valid. It exports the executor's identity\n(issue #33) into the adapter's environment as GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and\nGIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL, set by the product and never the tenant's git\nconfig, then invokes the named adapter (adapters/<name>/run) with the\nspec, the corpus, and the branch. It refuses (status refused) a commit\nbetween start_sha and HEAD not authored by that identity, checks that\nevery path touched matches a spec claim, records the adapter's own\ndeclared \"reports\" -- the fields adapters/<name>/conformance.json says\nit can supply with a real value (issue #41), so a field it claims and\nnever supplies is a defect the conformance suite catches rather than a\nsilent null -- then runs the criteria, the\ntests [tests].select and [tests].run name for the touched paths, and --\nwhen the manifest declares [checks].command -- the tenant's own\nwhole-tree check, from the tenant root. pass requires every criterion,\nthe test run, and the tenant's checks (if declared) to exit 0; any\nnon-zero exit iterates, with the failure as feedback, up to a fixed\nbudget. [checks] is optional; a tenant that declares none is not\nrefused. It writes the next build-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with\nthe adapter's transcript -- each iteration's gate output (criteria\nexits, the selected tests' stdout, the tenant's checks' tail) appended\nunder an \"--- attavo gates, iteration N ---\" heading, issue #89 -- beside\nit as build-NN.log. Every record whose status is not pass carries stop:\n{class, provenance, detail}, derived from the refusal, halted, and log\nalready on hand (issue #89); a pass record carries stop: null. See the\nbuild contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the full rules it\nenforces.\n\nverify refuses (exit 1) unless the item's latest build record has\nstatus pass, and unless the manifest declares [forge].checks_command --\na tenant command, taking a full commit sha on argv, that prints one\nline per check as \"<name> <conclusion>\". verify runs it on the build\nrecord's sha first: any conclusion other than success, neutral, or\nskipped writes verify-NN.json with status returned and calls no\nadapter, because a judge is never spent on a tree the forge already\ncalled red. With the forge green, verify calls the adapter named by\n[executor].verify (defaulting to [executor].build) with the diff since\nthe build's approval, the spec, and the build record, and records its\nfindings and its declared \"reports\" (issue #41). [executor.<adapter>.<stage>] shadows [executor.<adapter>] for\nbuild or verify alone; both merge parent then stage before setting\nATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG, and the record's adapter_config is the merged\nresult. Like build, every verify record whose status is not pass\ncarries stop: {class, provenance, detail} (issue #89); a pass record\ncarries stop: null. file-findings opens one tenant issue per finding in\nthe item's latest verify record via [forge].file_issue_command, and\nrefuses (exit 1, nothing filed) a record carrying a finding with no\nretires. See the verify contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the\nfull rules both enforce.\n\nfile-stops opens one tenant issue per stop record of the item with no\nissue filed for it yet, through [forge].file_issue_command, naming the\nclass, the provenance, the record path, and the log's last twenty\nlines; a record it has already filed carries a <stage>-NN.filed marker\nbeside it, holding the filing command's own stdout, so a second run\nfiles nothing new. Like a build or verify record, this command writes\nthe marker and leaves it uncommitted -- drive commits it, in the same\ncommit as the record it names (issue #89). It refuses (exit 1,\nnothing filed) a stop whose class is unclassed and whose detail is\nempty -- a stop the product cannot even describe is not filed as if it\ncould. See issue #89's lane for the full rules it enforces.\n\ncounsel reads the item's latest non-pass build or verify record -- or,\nwhen neither exists, its latest refused spec-gate record, the earliest\npoint a question can be answered inside the product, before any\nCRITERION_TIMEOUT = 120\nRECORD_RE = re.compile(r\"^([a-z]+)-([0-9]{2,})\\.json$\")\nBUILD_ITERATION_BUDGET = 3\nBUILD_HALT_EXIT = 3\nCHECKS_FEEDBACK_TAIL_LINES = 200\nPRODUCT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n# issue #84: a constant the lane names, not a manifest key, until a tenant\n# disagrees -- how long drive gives a forge's checks room to conclude\n# before it gives up and stops rather than call a judge on a tree the\n# forge has not yet finished reading. Tenant zero's own checks conclude\n# about five minutes after a push; the default bound gives them room to\n# finish so a person is not the one re-running drive after CI, which is\n# exactly the transport act this lane retires. ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S\n# and ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S, read at call time rather than once at\n# import, are for a test's own clock, not a tenant's -- there is no\n# manifest key for either.\nDRIVE_FORGE_POLL_BOUND_DEFAULT_S = 600.0\nDRIVE_FORGE_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT_S = 20.0\n\n\ndef drive_forge_poll_bound_s() -> float:\n    return float(os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S\", DRIVE_FORGE_POLL_BOUND_DEFAULT_S))\n\n\ndef drive_forge_poll_interval_s() -> float:\n    return float(os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S\", DRIVE_FORGE_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT_S))\n\n\nclass Proof:\n    def __init__(self, key: str, title: str) -> None:\n        self.key = key\n        self.title = title\n        self.holds = False\n        self.reason = \"\"\n        self.extra: dict = {}\n\n    def fail(self, reason: str, **extra) -> \"Proof\":\n        self.holds, self.reason = False, reason\n        self.extra.update(extra)\n        return self\n\n    def hold(self, reason: str, **extra) -> \"Proof\":\n        self.holds, self.reason = True, reason\n        self.extra.update(extra)\n        return self\n\n    def as_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return {\"proof\": self.key, \"title\": self.title,\n                \"holds\": self.holds, \"reason\": self.reason, **self.extra}\n\n\n               \"environment\", \"gate\", \"died\", \"hung\")\nSTOP_PROVENANCES = (\"product\", \"tenant\", \"executor\", \"spec\")\n\n# Beyond the enum spelling itself, the prose issue #88 actually shipped\n# (adapters/claude-code/run and adapters/codex/run, on main since\n# v0.16.0) once put a class's own name, or a real specimen's wording of\n# it, in the transcript for the generic match below to find. Issue #94\n# moves non-question and outlived-invocation onto report_class instead\n# (below): non-question's own halt line (\"halted: class non-question\")\n# would otherwise still satisfy the bare-name match here with no adapter\n# report-line field involved at all, and outlived-invocation's refusal\n# never named its class in text to begin with, so both are disabled here\n# -- the same pattern issue #93 established for ceiling, just below,\n# rather than removed outright.\nCLASS_TEXT_MARKERS: dict[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {\n    \"non-question\": (),\n    \"outlived-invocation\": (),\n    # Issue #93: ceiling's own text-based check is CEILING_MARKERS, below,\n    # with provenance \"product\" -- a fact about the tool, not an executor\n    # judgment like non-question/outlived-invocation are. Left at the\n    # default (the class's own name, \"ceiling\"), the generic match above\n    # would instead catch adapters/codex/run's and\n    # adapters/claude-code/run's own pre-emptive refusal -- which must\n    # carry the word \"ceiling\" by the same issue's own brief -- as\n    # provenance \"executor\", before CEILING_MARKERS is ever consulted.\n    \"ceiling\": (),\n    # A genuine question (issue #100's own followups) is read structurally\n    # -- status \"halted\" carrying a non-empty halted.question -- not by\n    # scanning for the literal word \"question\", which the question's own\n    # text very often contains regardless of what it is actually asking.\n    # Left at the default, the generic match above would misclassify any\n    # question that happens to use the word \"question\" as executor\n    # provenance, before the structural check in derive_stop is reached.\n    \"question\": (),\n    # environment/tenant (issue #115) is set directly by cmd_build's own\n    # preflight -- the one caller who knows a [checks].command exited 2\n    # on the approved tree -- never derived from adapter text. Left at\n    # the default, the generic match above would catch the word\n    # \"environment\" anywhere in a log or refusal (e.g. codex's own\n    # OPENAI_API_KEY auth-mismatch refusal, adapters/codex/run's\n    # check_auth) as an environment/executor stop that never happened.\n    \"environment\": (),\n}\n\n# Known tool error text for a declared ceiling -- issue #86's own specimen\n# (codex's \"Input exceeds...\" line on a diff too large to judge) is\n# \"input_too_large\"; a matching line anywhere in the log, not only its\n# last line, since cmd_build and cmd_verify both append \"[adapter exited\n# N]\" after whatever the tool itself printed. \"ceiling exceeded\" is issue\n# #93's own addition: both adapters now refuse pre-emptively, before the\n# tool is ever invoked, against a declared or fixed input limit, and\n+\n+def test_doctor_proof_six_says_not_read_when_the_store_cannot_be_read(tmp_path):\n+    \"\"\"Exit 2 from the attestation command (gh unauthenticated on a\n+    runner, the command missing) is \"the store could not be read\", never\n+    \"unsealed\": the item lands in not_read and the reason names the\n+    command and its exit.\"\"\"\n+    root, m1, m2 = _tenant_with_two_merged_items(tmp_path)\n+    (root / \"fake-attest\").write_text('#!/bin/sh\\nread sha\\necho \"gh: not logged in\" >&2\\nexit 2\\n')\n+    p = _proof(root)\n+    assert not p[\"holds\"]\n+    assert \"not read\" in p[\"reason\"] and \"exited 2\" in p[\"reason\"]\n+    assert p[\"not_read\"] == [\"1\", \"2\"] and p[\"unsealed\"] == [] and p[\"sealed\"] == []\n+\n+\n+def test_doctor_proof_six_fails_without_an_attestation_command(tmp_path):\n+    root = tmp_path / \"bare\"\n+    root.mkdir()\n+    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"init\", \"-q\", \"-b\", \"main\", \".\"], cwd=root, check=True)\n+    (root / \"attavo.toml\").write_text('[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n')\n+    (root / \"records\").mkdir()\n+    _git(root, \"config\", \"user.email\", \"doctor@attavo.invalid\")\n+    _git(root, \"config\", \"user.name\", \"doctor fixture\")\n+    _git(root, \"add\", \".\")\n+    _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"install\")\n+    _set_default_branch_ref(root)\n+    p = _proof(root)\n+    assert not p[\"holds\"] and \"attestation_command\" in p[\"reason\"]\ndiff --git a/bin/attavo b/bin/attavo\nindex 5083790..a80e1ef 100755\n--- a/bin/attavo\n+++ b/bin/attavo\n@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@\n     attavo ledger [N] [--json]\n     attavo stops [N] [--json]\n \n-The doctor is the definition of done. It asserts four proofs against a\n+The doctor is the definition of done. It asserts five proofs against a\n tenant root and exits 1 until every proof holds:\n \n   1. every-gate-rejects      every gate in the manifest's [gates] table,\n@@ -42,6 +42,16 @@ tenant root and exits 1 until every proof holds:\n                              adapter exit ended the log -- records before\n                              record_version 3 are counted and reported,\n                              never refused\n+  5. every-attested-item-is-sealed\n+                             every merged item that carries a record for\n+                             every stage has a statement in the forge's\n+                             attestation store for its merge commit, read\n+                             through [forge].attestation_command -- a\n+                             merge at or before [forge].sealed_since is\n+                             named as before the window instead of failed.\n+                             [forge].attestation_command exiting 2 means\n+                             the store itself could not be read, reported\n+                             as not_read by item and never as unsealed\n \n Nothing in doctor is a gate. The doctor reads; it never writes and it never\n blocks a merge by itself. It is what CI runs to say whether the product\n@@ -1428,13 +1438,103 @@ def proof_no_stop_lacks_cause(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\n                  older_records=older)\n \n \n+def attestation_command(m: dict) -> str | None:\n+    \"\"\"[forge].attestation_command: the tenant's own read of the store,\n+    given a merge sha on stdin, printing the statement as JSON on exit 0\n+    and nothing on a non-zero exit. Absent is not passing (issue #158:\n+    the doctor said done while #106, #148, #153 had no statement in the\n+    store at all -- there was no key to read one through).\"\"\"\n+    cmd = (m.get(\"forge\") or {}).get(\"attestation_command\")\n+    return cmd if isinstance(cmd, str) and cmd.strip() else None\n+\n+\n+def statement_for(root: Path, cmd: str, merge_sha: str) -> tuple[dict | None, int]:\n+    \"\"\"The statement the forge holds for merge_sha and the command's exit\n+    code. The statement is None when the command exits non-zero or prints\n+    anything but a JSON object -- exit 2 means the store itself could not\n+    be read (issue #158, amended after build-05: distinct from exit 1,\n+    the store read fine and simply held no statement).\"\"\"\n+    run = subprocess.run(cmd, shell=True, cwd=str(root), input=merge_sha + \"\\n\",\n+                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n+    if run.returncode != 0:\n+        return None, run.returncode\n+    try:\n+        parsed = json.loads(run.stdout)\n+    except ValueError:\n+        return None, run.returncode\n+    return (parsed if isinstance(parsed, dict) else None), run.returncode\n+\n+\n+def _is_ancestor(root: Path, earlier: str, later: str) -> bool:\n+    run = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", earlier, later],\n+                         capture_output=True, check=False)\n+    return run.returncode == 0\n+\n+\n+def proof_every_attested_item_is_sealed(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\n+    p = Proof(\"every-attested-item-is-sealed\", \"every attested item has its statement in the store\")\n+    if m is None:\n+        return p.fail(f\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no records directory is declared\")\n+    cmd = attestation_command(m)\n+    if cmd is None:\n+        return p.fail(\"no [forge].attestation_command in the manifest; the store cannot be read\")\n+    records_rel = m.get(\"paths\", {}).get(\"records\", \"\")\n+    records_dir = root / records_rel\n+    if not records_dir.is_dir():\n+        return p.fail(f\"no records directory under {records_dir}\")\n+    items = load_records(records_dir)\n+    complete = [item for item, stages in sorted(items.items()) if all(s in stages for s in STAGES)]\n+\n+    # [forge].sealed_since: merges at or before this sha predate the\n+    # tenant's merge queue -- the self-tenant's own #106, #148, #153 were\n+    # merged direct, with no merge_group run to seal them. They are\n+    # named, never failed, the same window convention proof three keeps\n+    # for commits before the manifest's own install.\n+    since = (m.get(\"forge\") or {}).get(\"sealed_since\")\n+    merges, refusal = _merges_reachable(root)\n+    if refusal:\n+        return p.fail(refusal)\n+    sealed: list[str] = []\n+    before_window: list[str] = []\n+    unsealed: list[str] = []\n+    not_merged: list[str] = []\n+    not_read: list[str] = []\n+    reasons: list[str] = []\n+    for item in complete:\n+        merge_sha, _ = merge_introducing_records(root, records_rel, item, STAGES, merges=merges)\n+        if merge_sha is None:\n+            not_merged.append(item)\n+            continue\n+        if isinstance(since, str) and since.strip() and _is_ancestor(root, merge_sha, since):\n+            before_window.append(item)\n+            continue\n+        statement, exit_code = statement_for(root, cmd, merge_sha)\n+        if statement is not None:\n+            sealed.append(item)\n+        elif exit_code == 2:\n+            not_read.append(item)\n+            reasons.append(f\"item {item} merged at {merge_sha[:12]}: not read -- \"\n+                           f\"the store could not be read; {cmd!r} exited 2\")\n+        else:\n+            unsealed.append(item)\n+            reasons.append(f\"item {item} merged at {merge_sha[:12]} has no statement in the store\")\n+    if reasons:\n+        return p.fail(\"; \".join(reasons), sealed=sealed, before_window=before_window,\n+                      unsealed=unsealed, not_merged=not_merged, not_read=not_read)\n+    return p.hold(f\"{len(sealed)} merged item(s) sealed, {len(before_window)} before the window, \"\n+                 f\"{len(not_merged)} not merged\",\n+                 sealed=sealed, before_window=before_window, unsealed=unsealed,\n+                 not_merged=not_merged, not_read=not_read)\n+\n+\n def doctor(root: Path) -> list[Proof]:\n     m = read_manifest(root)\n     return [proof_every_gate_rejects(root, m),\n             proof_one_item_every_stage(root, m),\n             proof_no_commit_lacks_record(root, m),\n             proof_no_stop_lacks_cause(root, m),\n-            proof_no_invocation_lacks_record(root, m)]\n+            proof_no_invocation_lacks_record(root, m),\n+            proof_every_attested_item_is_sealed(root, m)]\n \n \n def cmd_doctor(argv: list[str]) -> int:\ndiff --git a/schema/manifest.schema.json b/schema/manifest.schema.json\nindex 1f7fe52..b37b069 100644\n--- a/schema/manifest.schema.json\n+++ b/schema/manifest.schema.json\n@@ -88,6 +88,16 @@\n           \"type\": \"string\",\n           \"description\": \"Reads one finding as JSON on stdin and files it as a tenant issue. attavo file-findings runs it once per finding in the item's latest verify record.\",\n           \"minLength\": 1\n+        },\n+        \"attestation_command\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"description\": \"Reads a merge commit sha on stdin and prints that merge's attestation statement as JSON on exit 0; nothing on a non-zero exit. The doctor's fifth proof runs it once per merged, fully-staged item to require a statement in the store.\",\n+          \"minLength\": 1\n+        },\n+        \"sealed_since\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"description\": \"A commit sha. A merge at or before it predates the tenant's merge queue and is named by the doctor's fifth proof as before the window rather than failed.\",\n+          \"minLength\": 7\n         }\n       }\n     },\ndiff --git a/tests/test_doctor.py b/tests/test_doctor.py\nindex 37c82de..b3869ca 100644\n--- a/tests/test_doctor.py\n+++ b/tests/test_doctor.py\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n-\"\"\"The doctor's four proofs, as tests written before the capability.\n+\"\"\"The doctor's five proofs, as tests written before the capability.\n \n-Each test asserts that one proof holds against this repository. All four\n+Each test asserts that one proof holds against this repository. All five\n fail at the first commit and must fail: that is the definition of done,\n stated before anything exists to satisfy it. A test here turns green only\n when the capability it names has landed and been used for real.\n@@ -68,6 +68,15 @@ def test_no_invocation_lacks_record():\n     assert p[\"holds\"], p[\"reason\"]\n \n \n+def test_every_attested_item_is_sealed():\n+    \"\"\"Proof 5, issue #158. Every merged, fully-staged item has a\n+    statement in the forge's attestation store for its merge commit --\n+    #106, #148, #153 predate [forge].sealed_since and are named before the\n+    window instead.\"\"\"\n+    p = run_doctor(ROOT)[\"every-attested-item-is-sealed\"]\n+    assert p[\"holds\"], p[\"reason\"]\n+\n+\n def test_record_loader_uses_highest_attempt_number(tmp_path):\n     \"\"\"Acceptance 2a. <stage>-NN.json files are one stage's attempts; the\n     doctor treats the highest NN as latest, and STAGES is unchanged.\ndiff --git a/tests/test_doctor_sealed.py b/tests/test_doctor_sealed.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..3a3bb25\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/tests/test_doctor_sealed.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,169 @@\n+\"\"\"The doctor's fifth proof: every attested item has its statement in the\n+store (issue #158). This repository's own #106, #148, #153 were merged\n+direct, with no merge_group run and so no statement, and the doctor said\n+done anyway -- proof two held on the four stage records with the chain\n+held, never asking whether the merge was sealed.\n+\n+Run: python3 -m pytest tests -q\n+\"\"\"\n+import json\n+import subprocess\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n+ATTAVO = ROOT / \"bin\" / \"attavo\"\n+\n+FAKE_ATTEST = (\n+    '#!/bin/sh\\nread sha\\ngrep -qx \"$sha\" sealed.txt && printf %s '\n+    '\"{\\\\\"_type\\\\\": \\\\\"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1\\\\\"}\"\\n'\n+)\n+\n+\n+def _git(root: Path, *args: str) -> str:\n+    return subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), *args], capture_output=True, text=True,\n+                          check=True).stdout.strip()\n+\n+\n+def _tenant_with_two_merged_items(tmp_path: Path) -> tuple[Path, str, str]:\n+    root = tmp_path / \"sealed\"\n+    root.mkdir()\n+    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"init\", \"-q\", \"-b\", \"main\", \".\"], cwd=root, check=True)\n+    _git(root, \"config\", \"user.email\", \"doctor@attavo.invalid\")\n+    _git(root, \"config\", \"user.name\", \"doctor fixture\")\n+    (root / \"attavo.toml\").write_text(\n+        '[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n\\n[forge]\\nattestation_command = \"sh ./fake-attest\"\\n')\n+    (root / \"fake-attest\").write_text(FAKE_ATTEST)\n+    (root / \"sealed.txt\").write_text(\"\")\n+    _git(root, \"add\", \".\")\n+    _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"install\")\n+    merges = []\n+    for item in (\"1\", \"2\"):\n+        _git(root, \"checkout\", \"-q\", \"-b\", f\"attavo/{item}-x\")\n+        (root / \"records\" / item).mkdir(parents=True)\n+        for stage in (\"spec\", \"approval\", \"build\", \"verify\"):\n+            (root / \"records\" / item / f\"{stage}-01.json\").write_text('{\"status\": \"pass\"}')\n+            _git(root, \"add\", \"records\")\n+            _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", f\"{stage} record for item {item}\")\n+        _git(root, \"checkout\", \"-q\", \"main\")\n+        _git(root, \"merge\", \"-q\", \"--no-ff\", \"-m\", f\"Merge branch 'attavo/{item}-x'\", f\"attavo/{item}-x\")\n+        merges.append(_git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"))\n+    _git(root, \"update-ref\", \"refs/remotes/origin/main\", _git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"main\"))\n+    _git(root, \"symbolic-ref\", \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD\", \"refs/remotes/origin/main\")\n+    return root, merges[0], merges[1]\n+\n+\n+def _tenant_with_one_merged_and_one_unmerged_item(tmp_path: Path) -> Path:\n+    root = tmp_path / \"unmerged\"\n+    root.mkdir()\n+    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"init\", \"-q\", \"-b\", \"main\", \".\"], cwd=root, check=True)\n+    _git(root, \"config\", \"user.email\", \"doctor@attavo.invalid\")\n+    _git(root, \"config\", \"user.name\", \"doctor fixture\")\n+    (root / \"attavo.toml\").write_text(\n+        '[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n\\n[forge]\\nattestation_command = \"sh ./fake-attest\"\\n')\n+    (root / \"fake-attest\").write_text(FAKE_ATTEST)\n+    (root / \"sealed.txt\").write_text(\"\")\n+    _git(root, \"add\", \".\")\n+    _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"install\")\n+    _git(root, \"checkout\", \"-q\", \"-b\", \"attavo/1-x\")\n+    (root / \"records\" / \"1\").mkdir(parents=True)\n+    for stage in (\"spec\", \"approval\", \"build\", \"verify\"):\n+        (root / \"records\" / \"1\" / f\"{stage}-01.json\").write_text('{\"status\": \"pass\"}')\n+        _git(root, \"add\", \"records\")\n+        _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", f\"{stage} record for item 1\")\n+    _git(root, \"checkout\", \"-q\", \"main\")\n+    _git(root, \"merge\", \"-q\", \"--no-ff\", \"-m\", \"Merge branch 'attavo/1-x'\", \"attavo/1-x\")\n+    m1 = _git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")\n+    (root / \"sealed.txt\").write_text(m1 + \"\\n\")\n+    _git(root, \"add\", \"sealed.txt\")\n+    _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"seal item 1\")\n+    _git(root, \"checkout\", \"-q\", \"-b\", \"attavo/2-x\")\n+    (root / \"records\" / \"2\").mkdir(parents=True)\n+    for stage in (\"spec\", \"approval\", \"build\", \"verify\"):\n+        (root / \"records\" / \"2\" / f\"{stage}-01.json\").write_text('{\"status\": \"pass\"}')\n+        _git(root, \"add\", \"records\")\n+        _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", f\"{stage} record for item 2\")\n+    _git(root, \"checkout\", \"-q\", \"--detach\")\n+    _git(root, \"merge\", \"-q\", \"--no-ff\", \"-m\", \"synthetic test merge of attavo/2-x into main\", \"main\")\n+    return root\n+\n+\n+def _proof(root: Path) -> dict:\n+    run = subprocess.run([\"python3\", str(ATTAVO), \"doctor\", \"--json\", str(root)],\n+                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n+    proofs = json.loads(run.stdout)[\"proofs\"]\n+    return [p for p in proofs if p[\"proof\"] == \"every-attested-item-is-sealed\"][0]\n+\n+\n+def test_doctor_proof_six_fails_on_an_unsealed_merge(tmp_path):\n+    root, m1, m2 = _tenant_with_two_merged_items(tmp_path)\n+    (root / \"sealed.txt\").write_text(m1 + \"\\n\")\n+    p = _proof(root)\n+    assert not p[\"holds\"]\n+    assert \"item 2\" in p[\"reason\"] and m2[:12] in p[\"reason\"]\n+    assert p[\"sealed\"] == [\"1\"] and p[\"unsealed\"] == [\"2\"]\n+\n+\n+def test_doctor_proof_six_holds_when_every_merge_is_sealed(tmp_path):\n+    root, m1, m2 = _tenant_with_two_merged_items(tmp_path)\n+    (root / \"sealed.txt\").write_text(m1 + \"\\n\" + m2 + \"\\n\")\n+    p = _proof(root)\n+    assert p[\"holds\"] and p[\"sealed\"] == [\"1\", \"2\"]\n+\n+\n+def test_doctor_proof_six_names_a_merge_before_the_window_without_failing(tmp_path):\n+    root, m1, m2 = _tenant_with_two_merged_items(tmp_path)\n+    (root / \"sealed.txt\").write_text(m2 + \"\\n\")\n+    (root / \"attavo.toml\").write_text(\n+        '[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n\\n[forge]\\nattestation_command = \"sh ./fake-attest\"\\n'\n+        f'sealed_since = \"{m1}\"\\n')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
